metadata/_sms_note = "Pass 142: the Cheep Cheep (Puku Puku), Ricco Harbor's fish. Kind = Leaper: this node is the LAUNCH PAD -- put it in the water at the surface, turned the way the fish should fly (the node's yaw); the fish rises from under it, leaps in an arc (Launch pad: LaunchSpeedUnits = how hard, LaunchPitchDegrees = how steep), splashes down, loops under the surface, swims back to the pad and leaps again, forever. One that lands on a dock bounces, flops about (its touch hurts) and dies after 13 s; one that hits Mario in the air falls and dies; the hose in the air flings it away and it falls into the water, dead -- the pad then launches a new one (RelaunchTicks 1 = at once, as the game; with ReturnsToPad off every LaunchIntervalTicks). Kind = Swimmer: it swims under the surface from point to point (a Graph of Node3D children, or within WanderRadiusUnits of its place), bobbing; it hurts a swimming Mario it touches (set RelaunchTicks -1 for one that stays dead). Knobs: Launch pad, Deviations (DiveDepthUnits, Bounces, SpeedScale), Effects (the water column, the swim bubbles, the flop drops), Sounds (slots)."

